Description: CVE-2025-59250 - Secure Common Name parsing to prevent TLS hostname
 verification bypass in the Microsoft JDBC Driver for SQL Server. The previous
 parseCommonName(String) walked the "canonical" DN text by hand and could be
 tricked into returning a CN embedded inside another RDN attribute value (for
 example "OU=CN\=target.com, CN=attacker.com"), allowing an attacker to spoof
 the expected host name. This backports the upstream fix (PR #2802 / release
 10.2.4, commit 6c4c64113b92490357977f3e4f3bf5557e17a645) which parses the
 subject DN structurally with javax.naming.ldap.LdapName/Rdn and extracts the
 real CN RDN, and adds a regression test proving the spoofing attempt is
 rejected.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/microsoft/mssql-jdbc/commit/6c4c64113b92490357977f3e4f3bf5557e17a645
